research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-140-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-141-**Given:** A continuous map $f:X\to Y$ with $X$ nonempty compact Hausdorff and $Y$ uniform.
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-142-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md:143:[L1] A compact Hausdorff space has one compatible uniformity ([[thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-144-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-145-[L2] Continuity means that every neighbourhood of $f(x)$ contains the image of some neighbourhood of $x$, while uniform continuity is the entourage condition ([[def-continuous-map-top]], [[def-uniformly-continuous-map]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-146-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-147-[L3] Every entourage ball is a neighbourhood in the induced topology ([[thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology]]). Every open cover of a nonempty compact Hausdorff space is uniform ([[thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity]]), and every uniform cover has an entourage-ball cover refining it ([[lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary]]); every target entourage has a symmetric square root ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-148-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-149-## Proof
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-150-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-151-**Proof technique:** direct.
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-152-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-153-1.1 Let $V$ be a target entourage and choose a symmetric $W$ with $W^{-1}\circ W=W^{\circ2}\subseteq V$. For each $x\in X$, let $O_x$ be the union of all open sets $O$ such that $x\in O$ and $f[O]\subseteq W[f(x)]$. Continuity makes this family nonempty, and its union is an open neighbourhood of $x$ satisfying $f[O_x]\subseteq W[f(x)]$. [L2, L3, construct]
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-154-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.md-155-2.1 The open cover $(O_x)_{x\in X}$ is uniform by [L3]. Hence there is a source entourage $E$ whose ball cover refines it: for each $a\in X$, some $O_x$ contains $E[a]$. [step 1.1, L1, L3]
