research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.prompt.md-204-1.1 Let $V$ be a target entourage and choose a symmetric $W$ with $W^{-1}\circ W=W^{\circ2}\subseteq V$. For each $x\in X$, let $O_x$ be the union of all open sets $O$ such that $x\in O$ and $f[O]\subseteq W[f(x)]$. Continuity makes this family nonempty, and its union is an open neighbourhood of $x$ satisfying $f[O_x]\subseteq W[f(x)]$. [L2, L3, construct]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.prompt.md-205-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.prompt.md-206-2.1 The open cover $(O_x)_{x\in X}$ is uniform by [L3]. Hence there is a source entourage $E$ whose ball cover refines it: for each $a\in X$, some $O_x$ contains $E[a]$. [step 1.1, L1, L3]
