research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-212-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-213-**Given:** A continuous map $f:X\to Y$ with $X$ nonempty compact Hausdorff and $Y$ uniform.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-214-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log:215:[L1] A compact Hausdorff space has one compatible uniformity ([[thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-216-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-217-[L2] Continuity means that every neighbourhood of $f(x)$ contains the image of some neighbourhood of $x$, while uniform continuity is the entourage condition ([[def-continuous-map-top]], [[def-uniformly-continuous-map]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-218-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-219-[L3] Every entourage ball is a neighbourhood in the induced topology ([[thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology]]). Every open cover of a nonempty compact Hausdorff space is uniform ([[thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity]]), and every uniform cover has an entourage-ball cover refining it ([[lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary]]); every target entourage has a symmetric square root ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-final-cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous.log-220-
