research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:313805:+- `thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity` L3 says a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313806-+  compatible uniformity induces the given topology but cites
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313807-+  `def-uniform-space-by-entourages`, which does not define compatibility. Add
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313808-+  `def-uniformizable-space` and quote its compatible-uniformity clause.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313809-+- `thm-countably-based-uniformity-is-pseudometrizable` L3 says a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313810-+  pseudometric is a metric exactly when its zero-pair relation is diagonal,
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313811-+  but neither current target states the pseudometric-to-metric criterion. Add
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313812-+  `def-metric-space`, whose pseudometric clause states it exactly.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313813-+- `lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics` step
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313814-+  1.1 asserts `p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|` is a pseudometric without a triangle
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313815-+  citation. Add `lem-of-triangle-inequality` and `lem-of-abs-value` and state
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313816-+  the direct substitution proving symmetry, reflexivity, and the triangle
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-313817-+  inequality.
